// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
// Donor: none for the shape -- the C is the shell's sum ABI for the two
//        applied sums it spells per instance, read off shell.tpl.c (2026-10-01):
//        `NovaOpt_<T>` by value (emit_option.nv names both of its shapes) and
//        `NovaRes_<T>_<E>` behind a pointer, `r->tag = NOVA_TAG_Result_Ok` in
//        every `nova_make_NovaRes_*`. The tag constants come from the mangling
//        door (P5).
// Role: backend A (layer 11) -- the tag test of a `match` arm whose scrutinee
//       is an APPLIED sum: renders the checker's decision (the recorded
//       instance type and the variant row the lowering chose); decides nothing.
// Used by: emit_match.nv (`@emit_tag_test`, the head of every variant arm).
// Guarded by: check-novac-differential.sh (fixtures match_applied_sum/,
//             byte-for-byte against the oracle), novac/src/pipeline/
//             match_applied_sum_test.nv (both spellings pinned in the C, with a
//             control), check-novac-shell-freshness.sh (the tag names are the
//             shell's).
//
// INTEROP, NAMED AS SUCH (goes the day novac emits the whole prelude): the
// PAYLOAD read needs no door here -- the lowering already reads an Option's
// payload through `.value` (`take_payload`) and every other sum's through the
// union `->payload.<Variant>._<i>` (`take_field`), and the second IS the
// shell's `NovaRes_` layout. What novac could not spell was the TEST: its own
// `NOVAC_TAG_<module><Sum>_<Variant>` names nothing in the shell's instances.

module novac.emit_c

import ../types.{TyId}
import ../builtins.{OPTION_SOME_VARIANT}
import ../sem.{VariantRow, raw_vrow, c_shell_tag}

/// The C condition "the scrutinee `scr` (a local of the applied sum `scr_ty`)
/// holds the variant `vrow`" -- for a sum `is_shell_applied_sum` admitted.
///
/// An Option asks the ONE Option door (both of its shapes; the pointer shape
/// has no tag at all). A Result is the shell's heap instance: the tag behind
/// `->`, named in the shell's namespace -- the same access `is_value_sum`
/// would choose for any sum with a payload (A4), written out because the
/// instance is the shell's and its placement is not ours to decide.
fn Emitter @applied_sum_tag_test(scr_ty TyId, scr str, vrow VariantRow) -> str {
    if @is_option_inst(scr_ty) {
        if @ctx.variant_rows[raw_vrow(vrow)].name == OPTION_SOME_VARIANT {
            return @option_some_test(scr_ty, scr)
        }
        return @option_none_test(scr_ty, scr)
    }
    "${scr}->tag == ${c_shell_tag(@ctx, vrow)}"
}
